WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.774
Visitors often need a way to write to you.

00:00:03.774 --> 00:00:08.975
The Forms module builds a contact form from widgets, on any page that holds widgets.

00:00:08.975 --> 00:00:12.904
In this video, let's enable it, build a form with fields and a

00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:14.580
button, and publish it.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.415
The Forms module provides widgets for building a form.

00:00:22.415 --> 00:00:26.566
The Form widget is the form itself, and the field widgets go inside it.

00:00:26.566 --> 00:00:30.178
The Form widget sits on a page that can hold widgets, such as

00:00:30.178 --> 00:00:32.280
the Page type of the Blog recipe.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:37.913
Input is a single-line field, and its type can be text, email, phone,

00:00:37.913 --> 00:00:39.801
number, date, and more.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:44.424
Text Area takes longer text, and Select offers a list of choices.

00:00:44.424 --> 00:00:47.810
Button sends the form when its type is Submit.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:53.209
Every field widget has an HTML Name, the name its value is sent under.

00:00:53.209 --> 00:00:57.798
Input, Text Area, and Select also have a label setting, which is None

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:01.040
until you change it, so a field shows no label.

00:01:05.306 --> 00:01:08.704
The Forms feature is listed under Tools, Features.

00:01:08.704 --> 00:01:11.616
Let's search for Forms, and select Enable.

00:01:12.076 --> 00:01:14.203
A notification confirms it.

00:01:14.203 --> 00:01:19.616
Forms relies on the Widgets and Flows features, which the Blog recipe enables.

00:01:20.086 --> 00:01:21.754
The form goes on a page.

00:01:21.754 --> 00:01:26.312
Under Content, Content Items, the New button lists the types you can create.

00:01:26.312 --> 00:01:27.646
Let's choose Page.

00:01:28.104 --> 00:01:30.545
A page has a title and a permalink.

00:01:30.545 --> 00:01:35.071
Let's enter Contact Us as the title, and leave the permalink empty, so

00:01:35.071 --> 00:01:37.274
it is generated from the title.

00:01:37.732 --> 00:01:40.631
Below the permalink is the list of widgets.

00:01:40.631 --> 00:01:44.062
The plus button, Add Widget, lists the widget types.

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:45.482
Let's choose Form.

00:01:45.949 --> 00:01:49.791
The form's title identifies it in the editor, and the page does not

00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:51.160
show it to visitors.

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.529
Let's enter Contact.

00:01:53.004 --> 00:01:56.142
Action is the address the form submits to.

00:01:56.142 --> 00:02:00.718
Method is POST or GET, and EncType sets how the data is encoded.

00:02:00.718 --> 00:02:05.294
Let's leave Action empty and keep the defaults of the other two.

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.875
Both checkboxes are selected.

00:02:07.875 --> 00:02:12.043
Anti Forgery Token adds a hidden token to the form, and Save Form

00:02:12.043 --> 00:02:17.150
Location stores the address of the page, so a workflow can send the visitor back.

00:02:17.618 --> 00:02:19.441
Let's select Save Draft.

00:02:19.441 --> 00:02:23.088
A notification confirms that the Page draft was saved.

00:02:27.284 --> 00:02:30.083
The page is open again, with its Form widget.

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:33.870
Fields go inside the form, so the Form widget has a plus button

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.462
of its own, Add Widget.

00:02:35.462 --> 00:02:36.834
Let's add an Input.

00:02:37.286 --> 00:02:39.039
HTML Name is required.

00:02:39.039 --> 00:02:43.859
It is the name the browser sends the value under, written with letters,

00:02:43.859 --> 00:02:47.866
digits, hyphens, underscores, periods, or square brackets.

00:02:47.866 --> 00:02:49.306
Let's enter Name.

00:02:49.757 --> 00:02:51.183
ID is optional.

00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:55.122
It sets the ID of the field on the page, and when it

00:02:55.122 --> 00:02:58.857
is empty, the ID is generated from the HTML Name.

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:01.554
Label option is None by default.

00:03:01.554 --> 00:03:06.328
Standard shows the label text before the field, and Screen Readers hides it

00:03:06.328 --> 00:03:09.099
visually but keeps it for screen readers.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:12.754
Let's choose Standard, and enter Name as the Label Text.

00:03:13.207 --> 00:03:14.272
Type is Text.

00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:18.703
Placeholder Text is what the empty field shows, and Default Value is what

00:03:18.703 --> 00:03:21.340
the field holds before the visitor types.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.537
Let's enter Your full name as the Placeholder Text.

00:03:24.991 --> 00:03:27.706
A second Input holds the email address.

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:32.231
Let's add it with the HTML Name Email, the Label option Standard, the

00:03:32.231 --> 00:03:37.661
Label Text Email address, the Type Email, and the Placeholder Text name@example.com.

00:03:38.119 --> 00:03:41.429
Let's select Save Draft to keep the two fields.

00:03:45.729 --> 00:03:48.616
The page opens again with both inputs.

00:03:48.616 --> 00:03:53.274
Add Widget, inside the form, lists Select, for a list of choices.

00:03:53.274 --> 00:03:58.064
Its HTML Name is Topic, its Label option is Standard, and its Label

00:03:58.064 --> 00:04:00.229
Text is What is this about.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:04.021
The Editor setting decides how the choices appear:

00:04:04.021 --> 00:04:07.698
as a Dropdown, as Checkbox options, or as Radio options.

00:04:07.698 --> 00:04:09.240
Let's keep Dropdown.

00:04:09.694 --> 00:04:15.104
Each option has a text, which visitors read, and a value, which the form sends.

00:04:15.104 --> 00:04:17.013
Let's add three options:

00:04:17.013 --> 00:04:20.259
General question, Support request, and Sales.

00:04:20.259 --> 00:04:21.404
The Default?

00:04:21.404 --> 00:04:26.304
column picks the option that starts selected, and let's leave it empty.

00:04:26.762 --> 00:04:29.128
A Text Area holds a longer message.

00:04:29.128 --> 00:04:33.456
Like the other fields, it has the HTML Name Message, the Label option

00:04:33.456 --> 00:04:36.745
Standard, and the Placeholder Text How can we help.

00:04:36.745 --> 00:04:39.862
Rows sets its height in lines, so let's use six.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.597
Last, a Button.

00:04:41.597 --> 00:04:45.613
Like the fields, it needs an HTML Name, so let's enter Send.

00:04:45.613 --> 00:04:49.993
Text is what visitors read on it, so let's enter Send message, and

00:04:49.993 --> 00:04:52.610
Type is Submit, which sends the form.

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:54.627
Let's select Publish.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.970
A notification confirms that the Page was published.

00:05:02.170 --> 00:05:04.680
The permalink was generated from the title:

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:05.551
contact-us.

00:05:05.551 --> 00:05:10.110
Let's open the page, where the form shows its widgets in the order they were added.

00:05:10.572 --> 00:05:15.590
Each label comes from its label text, and each empty field shows its placeholder.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.282
The Topic field is a dropdown list with the three options.

00:05:19.742 --> 00:05:22.716
Let's fill the form in with sample values:

00:05:22.716 --> 00:05:26.122
a name, an email address, a topic, and a message.

00:05:26.593 --> 00:05:30.493
The Send message button submits the form to the address in the Action

00:05:30.493 --> 00:05:32.209
field, which is empty here.

00:05:32.209 --> 00:05:37.513
Pointing it at something that receives the submission is a separate task from building the form.

00:05:39.513 --> 00:05:43.698
A page, a Form widget, and field widgets make a contact form.

00:05:43.698 --> 00:05:50.319
Separate videos cover validating what visitors type, and processing each submission with a workflow.

00:05:50.319 --> 00:05:51.943
Thanks for watching.

